tward movement, lifting the glass from the countertop. This lifting motion continues, with the right hand consistently raising the clear glass tumbler further upwards and progressively to the right, gradually moving it away from the immediate vicinity of the white placemat and ceramic plate. Throughout this entire progression, the person's left hand maintains its extended position on the black countertop to the left of the placemat, providing a stable anchor, with only a minor upward adjustment of the wrist observed in the final moments of the sequence. The person's gaze remains directed downwards towards the countertop area, following the trajectory of the lifted glass. [Ego view] **Scene Overview:** From the subject's inferred perspective, the immediate foreground is dominated by the black countertop with white speckles. On this countertop, directly in front of the subject, a white rectangular placemat with a patterned border is visible. Centered on the placemat is a white circular ceramic plate, which holds red pasta and orange beans or vegetables. A silver-colored metallic fork is visible to the left of the plate, and a silver-colored metallic knife is to the right. To the right of the plate, a clear glass tumbler is present. A dark-colored smartphone is also visible on the countertop, positioned towards the right edge of the placemat. The egocentric view shows a point cloud representation of the immediate environment, outlining the hands and objects with distinct reddish-brown dots, against a black background. **Action Analysis:** The sequence commences with the subject's right hand visible in the lower right portion of the field of view. The fingers of the right hand are extended downwards, positioned just above the clear glass tumbler, which rests on the black countertop next to the white plate of food. The white placemat is also clearly visible in the central-lower portion of the view. The left hand remains outside the egocentric frame. The action transition